{"step_index":78,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:32:29Z","content":"I have compiled the formal academic implementation report (~1,350 words) for the **StreamWave Serverless Media Platform** in [`academic_report.md`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/academic_report.md).\n\n---\n\n### 📄 Executive Summary & Key Report Highlights\n\n1. **Serverless Execution Architecture**:\n   FastAPI operates as an on-demand Vercel Serverless Function (Vercel 2024a, Vercel 2024b). Compute resources are instantiated ephemerally during HTTP requests, eliminating idle server costs.\n\n2. **Direct Edge Media Distribution**:\n   Demonstration media bytes are delivered directly to the user's browser via Vercel Edge CDN or Vercel Blob Storage (Vercel 2024d). Media bytes are never proxied through FastAPI application code.\n\n3. **Telemetry & Log Ingestion**:\n   Playback events posted to `POST /api/play-events` generate server-side UTC ISO 8601 timestamps and write structured JSON logs to standard output, captured via Vercel Runtime Logs (Vercel 2024c) without permanent database writes.\n\n4. **Enterprise Production Pathways**:\n   The report details how this non-commercial academic prototype on the Vercel Hobby plan would scale into an enterprise production environment by incorporating OAuth2/JWT authentication, persistent PostgreSQL databases, Kafka event streaming, signed CDN cookie protection, and adaptive HLS DRM video transcoding.\n\n5. **Formal Citations & Documentation**:\n   Includes Harvard-style in-text citations and a complete reference list citing official documentation sources from Vercel and FastAPI.\n\n---\n\n### 📂 Report Document Access\n\nThe full academic report is formatted in GitHub-flavored Markdown and is available at:\n👉 [`academic_report.md`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/academic_report.md)"}
