{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T15:32:51Z","content":"Here is the step-by-step guide to run and test the **StreamWave Serverless Media Platform** on your local machine.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Open Terminal & Navigate to Project Directory\n\nNavigate to the project directory containing [`app.py`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/app.py):\n\n```bash\ncd C:\\Users\\dell\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Create & Activate Virtual Environment\n\nCreate a clean Python 3.12 virtual environment:\n\n#### On Windows (PowerShell / Command Prompt):\n```powershell\npython -m venv .venv\n.\\.venv\\Scripts\\activate\n```\n\n#### On Linux / macOS:\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Install Required Dependencies\n\nInstall the pinned dependencies from [`requirements.txt`](file:///C:/Users/dell/.gemini/antigravity/brain/228fe0bc-0a77-489e-a1ba-57d617247457/requirements.txt):\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Generate the Demonstration Audio Asset\n\nSynthesize the 3-second non-copyrighted demonstration WAV audio file (`public/media/demo.wav`):\n\n```bash\npython scripts/generate_demo_audio.py\n```\n*(You should see: `✅ Demo WAV audio generated successfully at: .../public/media/demo.wav`)*\n\n---\n\n### 5. Run the Automated Test Suite\n\nExecute all 10 unit test cases using `pytest`:\n\n```bash\npytest tests/test_api.py -v\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```text\ntests/test_api.py::test_health_endpoint PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_get_complete_media_catalogue PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_vercel_blob_url_environment_injection PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_local_fallback_when_no_blob_env PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_media_search_filter_stream PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_media_type_filter_music PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_media_genre_filter PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_get_valid_media_detail_id_1 PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_get_unknown_media_detail_404 PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_valid_play_event PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_play_event_unknown_media_404 PASSED\ntests/test_api.py::test_play_event_invalid_body_422 PASSED\n\n========================== 12 passed in 0.45s ==========================\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Start the Local Server\n\nLaunch Uvicorn to serve the FastAPI backend and static web interface:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn app:app --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Interact & Test in Your Browser\n\nOpen your web browser and test the following URLs:\n\n| What to Test | URL | How to Verify |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **StreamWave Web App** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000) | 1. **Search**: Type `Cook` or `stream` in search box.<br>2. **Filters**: Click **Movies** or **Music** tabs, or choose a genre.<br>3. **Details Modal**: Click **ℹ Details** on any card.<br>4. **Audio Playback**: Click **▶ Play**; listen to audio and watch status dot change to **Event Logged**. |\n| **Health API** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health](http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health) | Returns JSON status: `{\"status\":\"ok\", \"platform\":\"StreamWave...\", ...}` |\n| **Media API** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media](http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media) | Returns full JSON list of 8 media items. |\n| **Music Filter API** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media?type=music](http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media?type=music) | Returns only music items (*Disappear*, *Mudhara Vachida*, etc.). |\n| **Single Item API** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media/1](http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media/1) | Returns item metadata for *Cook Off*. |\n| **Swagger API Docs** | [http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs) | Interactive Swagger UI allowing manual testing of all FastAPI endpoints. |\n\n---\n\n### 8. Testing Vercel Blob URL Ingestion (Optional)\n\nTo test Vercel Blob URL override locally, set `STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL` before running Uvicorn:\n\n#### On Windows PowerShell:\n```powershell\n$env:STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL=\"https://public.blob.vercel-storage.com/demo.wav\"\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```\n\n#### On Linux / macOS:\n```bash\nexport STREAMWAVE_BLOB_URL=\"https://public.blob.vercel-storage.com/demo.wav\"\nuvicorn app:app --reload\n```\n\nWhen you visit [http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media/1](http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/media/1), `media_url` will automatically show your configured Vercel Blob storage URL."}
